  "method": "for every frame and part: R(q_baked) * v_rest + t_baked against matrix_world @ local vertex of the keyed objects; max over all vertices (cm). float32 = arrays before the EXR; from_saved_exr = values re-read from the half float file (half float step: plain rounding of q and t costs up to ~0.06 cm; the script therefore stores, per frame and part, the float16 q (within one half step of exact) and float16 t (least squares) with the smallest max error, taking the worse of the normalised and not-renormalised quaternion use)",
